  "spoken_transcript": "Continuous vomiting and inability to drink require urgent care. A viral cold can irritate a baby's stomach, causing vomiting. Should you offer baby food, formula, or just rice porridge? Formula provides vital hydration and calories for sick babies. Mix formula to normal concentration, reduce the amount per feeding to two-thirds, and feed more frequently. After vomiting, keep offering small frequent formula or breast-milk feeds. The 4-to-6-hour pause applies to solids, not fluids. Lethargy or poor eye contact are serious warning signs. Hold your baby upright, supporting their head and trunk, for 30 minutes after vomiting. A persistent fever above 38°C needs medical attention. If symptoms worsen, consult your pediatrician without delay.",
